Lifetime: The variable exists for the entire duration of the program.

Initialization: If not explicitly initialized, they are initialized to zero (for global/static variables) or to the default value (for local static variables).

Usage:

Global static variables: Declared outside of any function, they are accessible only within the file where they are defined. They are not visible to other files, even if they are declared extern in other files.

Local static variables: Declared inside a function. They retain their value between function calls. They are initialized only once, during the first call to the function.

Example:

// Global static variable
